{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Decorator Pattern.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Decorator Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"decorator pattern decorator pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Decorator Pattern.md","fileName":"Decorator Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Decorator Pattern","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 22:12\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Object-Oriented Design Patterns]] [[Xamarin Application Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","Xamarin Application Architecture","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Decorator Pattern.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Decorator Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"decorator pattern decorator pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Decorator Pattern.md","fileName":"Decorator Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Decorator Pattern","heading":"Decorator Pattern","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A decorator implements the same interface as an object it wraps, delegates the core operation to that object, and adds behavior around it. The book's message decorators change console color while leaving simple or alert message classes responsible for their own output. Wrapping can be composed or selected at runtime, extending behavior without requiring a subclass for every combination of features.\n\nDecorator adds behavior by wrapping an object through a compatible interface, so the new responsibility can be composed at runtime without creating a subclass for every combination. The wrapper should preserve the wrapped object's established contract while adding its concern.","tags":["baby"],"